  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep bread and nuts: Preheat the oven to 200C. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Tear the baguette into 1cm chunks. Put the bread in a single layer on one half of the lined tray, drizzle with olive oil, season with salt and pepper and toss to coat. Put the hazelnuts on the other half of the tray.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495165/photos/large/prep_bread_and_nuts-98d56c99e6a8b2edce5f62d38bb11c35.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake croutons and nuts: Bake the bread and hazelnuts for 5-6 mins until the bread is golden and crisp and the hazelnuts are toasted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495166/photos/large/bake_croutons_and_nuts-a1f1cea2c2acb61391c8098af3815b61.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make slaw: Meanwhile, combine the country seasoning, 2 tbs mayonnaise and 1 tbs white wine vinegar in a large bowl. Peel the carrot (see Cooking tip). Shred the carrot and unpeeled apple using a julienne peeler or coarsely grate with a box grater (see Kitchen 101). Add the carrot, apple and salad leaves to the dressing and toss to coat. Season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495167/photos/large/make_slaw-b7ffda5c9c2797b4152d600a234bae09.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pan-fry haloumi: Thinly slice the haloumi. Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a medium frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the haloumi for 1-2 mins each side until golden. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495168/photos/large/pan_fry_haloumi-5080246c678ac4aabc771797bf220348.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the haloumi to the salad and toss to combine. Divide the salad among bowls, scatter over the hazelnuts and croutons and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495169/photos/large/serve_up-5cd0a8b00483a9d0a9de18730b907b9e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: If you don't have a julienne peeler, you might like to cut the apple and carrot into matchsticks using a sharp knife.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495170/photos/large/kitchen_101-82127f0f5c8c1063e25daad1e063bda2.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
